commit 6956102602b382c8be5b1779a14dcf0d7d3a0a7e
Author: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 28 06:03:09 2026 +0000

    midout: phase 3b reads each probe's digits once for two chunks
    
    Each lane now covers chunks q and q + 8 of one list entry (32 probe
    streams, one entry per lane per step) instead of chunk q of two
    entries. The digits are extracted and the row address is formed once
    per digit; the second chunk's rows are a constant offset away. Every
    (entry, chunk) word, mask and record is computed by the same formula
    as before; only which lane computes it, and so the records' order in
    a slab, changes. Same 32 entries x 16 chunks per cube step.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

